cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TRACE, please cite it as below. TRACE is a research prototype; none of its results have been checked by an outside party."
title: "TRACE: a memory that organizes itself (research prototype)"
type: software
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-04
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Anshul48/trace"
url: "https://anshul48.github.io/trace/"
authors:
  - name: "The TRACE team (GitHub: Anshul48)"
abstract: >-
  TRACE sorts a growing library into groups from the passages themselves, so a
  question wakes only a small part of it, and every answer carries a record
  that can be checked. On a sealed library of 812,545 passages (99.9 million
  tokens, short of the 100M target by 0.11%), a question scored 0.79% of the
  rows on one of four nearly equal parts and kept 0.9985 of exact search's top ten,
  over 50 test searches, with the team's own library and method. The tested
  engine is frozen (207 files, verifiable with tools/verify_freeze.py).
keywords:
  - memory for AI systems
  - semantic search
  - sparse activation
  - provenance
  - reproducibility
  - research prototype
